WEBVTT

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.730
One of the most enjoyable things
about traveling is the food!

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:36.290
Along the way, we found an
all-you-can-eat restaurant.

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.340
But, just when we were
ready to dig in...

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.200
...that crazy monster-worshipping
princess Martina showed up!

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:45.610
For some little thing I did to her
she put a curse on me as revenge...

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.510
...so I wasn't able
to eat anything at all!

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.070
Next time, I'm definitely
gonna eat my fill!

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.240
I'm really hungry...

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.210
Same with me.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.840
All right, then let's get
something to eat here!

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:25.610
Very well.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:26.950
Oh! Miss Lina!
Look at this!

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:30.790
The cuisine they have listed here...

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.480
Could... Could this be?!

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:33.990
The greatest, most sublime,
nearly legendary...

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:38.050
...example of gourmet cuisine
they call "The King of the Lunch!"

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:41.190
Also known as dragon cuisine!

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:45.900
If memory serves, it was
created as an unusual cuisine...

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:49.530
...designed for the mouths
of royalty in the court!

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.340
Especially when you
make it from lake dragon.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.850
With its mildly sweet
flavor and rich texture...

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:57.910
...they say it's the most
sublimely wonderful food of all...

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.880
...and the kings whose tongues
it graced would moan with joy.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.480
If you want to eat delicious
cuisine, I'll say it again.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.750
Dragon cuisine with lake dragon!

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.230
All right, it's settled!

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:12.290
For lunch today, we'll have a full-
course dragon feast!

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:22.970
Hi there!

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.630
Welcome!

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:30.810
What?! A full-course
dragon feast?!

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:34.440
Yeah, and they said
money was no object.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.780
Well? How many
of them are there?

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.880
Hmm... Four.
They look like travelers.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:44.830
Hmm... Travelers, huh?
Hey! Where's Ashford?

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.060
Sir! I haven't seen him.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:50.690
He's probably taking a
nap somewhere again.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:53.700
All right! We've still got some
orc and fresh whale meat...

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:54.800
...in the ice house, don't we?

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:56.970
Huh? You want
us to use THAT?

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.340
Look, it'll smell like
a rare dish, right?

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.640
They don't have to
know what they're eating!

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:05.650
Nobody's crazy enough to risk
their life just for dragon cuisine!

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:06.840
All right!
Don't screw this up!

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.290
Fight! Fight! Fight!

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.020
I wonder what kind of
food we'll get. I'm excited!

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:16.220
Don't hog all
the food, Gourry!

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:19.420
Well, you'd better leave
me some to eat, then!

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.160
Mr. Xellos, won't you eat with us?

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:25.490
That's all right.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:26.230
But...

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.930
Leave him be.

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:30.000
Sorry for the wait.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:34.640
Dragon's wine souffle...
Dragon's fin soup.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.110
Sukiyaki with
marbled dragon meat!

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:40.480
Oh, it's the full-course dragon
feast I've only dreamed about!

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:49.020
Well, then, let's eat!

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:59.200
What's wrong, Lina?

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:05.010
What is this stuff?!
It's so bad I can't eat it!

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:06.070
Think so?

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:08.580
I can eat this.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:12.410
The soup's been spiced
to hide the flavor!

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.450
This isn't what I expect
gourmet food to be!

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.820
How could you feed this
stuff to your customers?!

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:19.690
That's absolutely evil!

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:21.720
Take me to your chef.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:24.230
Y-Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.270
Hey, Lina?
Aren't you gonna eat this?

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:32.400
Heck, don't look a
gift horse in the mouth!

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:33.530
Okay!

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:36.170
Who's the chef?

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.940
Come on, tell me
who he really is!

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:42.850
This is no place for
amateurs to set foot into!

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:54.820
I'm Ashford, the chef
for this restaurant.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:58.260
What you call a kitchen is,
to a chef, his castle!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.560
And how dare you be so rude...

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:02.660
...as to come tracking
dirt into MY castle!

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:05.430
Oh, you're one to cop a
high and mighty attitude! You...

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.870
Hey, Lina! This is
the last of the food!

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.970
I know you'd hate to miss out,
so I'll share it with you!

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:15.170
My meat!

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.210
He's good!

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:22.410
My meat!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:28.090
Hey! I saved
that to eat last!

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.300
You guys tried to fool
our customers by using...

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:43.600
...that whale and orc meat we have
in the corner of the ice house!

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:45.710
What's with this
attitude of yours?!

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.750
After you made
this garbage for us...

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:51.280
Although I knew nothing of this...

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:54.680
...I apologize and
beg your forgiveness.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:58.480
Never mind that!
What about my poor stomach?!

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.080
It won't recover after getting
all set to eat dragon cuisine!

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.560
Very well! I, Ashford,
shall take responsibility for this...

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:08.930
...and will prepare a dragon
cuisine feast for you all!

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:09.870
Really?!

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:10.730
Of course!

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.500
All right! Dragon!
Dragon! Dragon cuisine!

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:23.240
We're after a lake dragon!
The finest food in this lake!

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:34.790
First, we raise
the anti-dragon net!

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:38.960
Anti-dragon net? Does it have
special features or something?

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:42.690
Of course! It's bigger
than normal to handle dragons!

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.400
That's it?

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:48.770
All right,
we'll cast our line here!

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.140
Drop anchor!

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:54.470
There isn't any anchor here.

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:59.310
Oops. I was so set on getting
my anti-dragon weaponry...

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:02.220
...that I totally
forgot to bring one!

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.550
Are you getting worried, too?

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:09.290
No choice. We'll have to use
something in place of the anchor.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:13.630
Say, Zel...
How much do you weigh?

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:16.260
Why are you asking me that?
You aren't going to!

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:19.330
Hey, wait! Come on, even you
wouldn't do that! Stop!

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:22.530
Amelia! Say something to her!

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.310
Poor Mr. Zelgadis...

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.510
We can at least let you
breathe down there.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:32.610
Oh, my. Oh, my.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:39.290
Zel! Don't move!
You're our anchor, remember?

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:03.580
- This sure hits the spot!
- Yeah, I was thirsty, too.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:08.480
Mr. Zelgadis!
We made some tea!

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:10.610
I'll give you some right now!

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:16.480
Miss Lina, Mr. Zelgadis is
trying to say something.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:18.430
What? What? What? Yikes!

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:22.900
It's here!

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:25.300
All right, now!
Raise the anchor!

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:33.570
It's huge!

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:35.440
It's for real!

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:37.980
It looks ready to eat!

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.950
All right! Dragon...

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:41.490
Don't!

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.450
Hey, come on!
Why'd you stop me?

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:52.830
You idiot! Slaying
a dragon with magic...

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.700
...is the worst
of all ways to get it!

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:56.230
In the name of my ancestors,
I won't allow you...

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:58.330
...to use such inelegant methods!

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.740
Huh? Really?

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.400
And while we're on
the subject...

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.490
So, is Zelgadis all right?

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:19.680
Oh, don't worry about him.
He's just a little waterlogged.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.450
But he went through so much!

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:24.520
Should we really
just leave him alone?

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.460
No, I suppose we
shouldn't do that.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:28.290
Maybe we could give
him artificial respiration.

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.800
Hmm... Oh, I suppose so.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:34.400
Right. We have no choice.
Well, then...

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:50.250
Just you wait, lake dragon!
I'll get you with my own hands!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.010
Well, we'll just have to make
do with this food for today.

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:15.350
But tomorrow we'll
definitely be dining on dragon!

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.620
No matter what happens?

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.950
Of course! For dragon cuisine,
the rarest dish in the world?

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.260
If I can't eat it,
what else can I hope to eat?!

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.060
Right, Gourry?

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.030
Doesn't really matter much to me...

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:30.670
Uh, I want it! I want it!
I want it! I want it!

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:35.070
And besides that,
I wonder where Amelia's gone.

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:45.310
Mr. Ashford?

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:48.980
Would you like to eat
some food? It's dinner.

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.390
It seems like you
have a reason for this.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:57.590
For what?

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:59.360
For making this dragon cuisine.

00:11:59.430 --> 00:12:03.200
Do you have a special
reason for doing this?

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:06.960
Years ago, I had a granddaughter.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:13.370
She was a very sickly child,
always ill with something.

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:20.050
She said to me "Just once,
I'd like to try dragon cuisine."

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:26.360
I decided to try and fulfill
her wish, so I set out.

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:32.860
You fool!

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:35.800
You'll never be able
to kill a dragon like that!

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:37.500
Yes, Master!

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:41.470
I became an apprentice to
a master of dragon cuisine.

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:45.640
Day after day, I practiced
intensely. And then, finally...

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.740
Go, Ashford!
As long as he has wisdom...

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:57.620
...and a fighting spirit,
nothing is impossible for a man!

00:12:57.690 --> 00:12:59.090
Yes, Master!

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:05.960
The dragon's weak spot
is the nape of its neck!

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:08.500
There's a nerve bundle there!

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:10.870
Yes, Master!

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:16.040
Secret Strike!
The Shooting Star Cleaver Slash!

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:25.680
But, after I'd finally
acquired the skill...

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.710
...when I returned to my kingdom...

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:31.590
...my dear granddaughter
had left this world.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:37.820
Since then, I've kept the
secrets of dragon cuisine to myself.

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:40.800
Then why are you helping us?

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:43.330
You see, my dear...

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:47.300
My dead granddaughter
looked just like you.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:52.500
Miss Lina...

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:56.210
Amelia, what's?

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:59.840
Oh, Miss Lina! Miss Lina!
We have to!

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.350
We just have to
catch that dragon!

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:05.720
We have to eat
that dragon cuisine!

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.060
So, he said you looked
like someone, right?

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:14.400
Yeah, his dead granddaughter...

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:18.300
He told me I looked
like his dead daughter.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:21.240
And I look like
his dead son-in-law!

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:23.000
And as for me...

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:27.510
...he said I look like his delicate
wife when she was young!

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:32.640
Oops.

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:55.000
Well, well... That's a
fairly elaborate plan.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.940
All right! Today we'll
drop anchor here!

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:10.320
Zel! Hang in there!

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:20.630
Now look, you guys!

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:22.390
Uh-oh...

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:28.140
Was there just a splash?

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:31.570
There it is!

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:34.580
Heh-heh! You fool!
You've walked right into our trap!

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:36.740
Well? Well?!
What do we do now?

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:39.880
You need to ask?! Next we...

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:41.940
I never thought
about that.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:00.430
Now look,
I've had enough of this!

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.470
My thoughts exactly.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:14.380
How cruel.

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:17.790
Next comes this!

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:18.750
What's that?

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:22.920
This is a fishing lure for
the end of a fishing line.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:26.260
Don't tell me you expect
to hook the dragon with that.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:28.820
For one thing, it's so small.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:32.560
Well, for a dragon we'll need
something big to catch its eye.

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:35.610
Something big to catch its eye...

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:45.440
We're counting on you, Gourry!

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:49.980
Well, then, now we just wait
for the dragon to take the bait.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:54.660
Simple is best.

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:30.760
It's here!

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.200
All right! Reel it in!

00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:39.500
Okay!

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:48.180
All right, we've got it!

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:12.060
Oh, God! God of Cookery!
Give me strength!

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:20.040
Secret Strike!
Shooting Star Cleaver Slash!

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:33.350
He got it!

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:35.660
All right!

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:42.330
Oh, my. Impressive.

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:05.020
We've got our ingredients.
Just you wait!

00:19:05.090 --> 00:19:07.680
I'm making the greatest
dragon cuisine ever!

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:11.090
So, what are we
gonna be eating first?

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:14.260
We'll start with
dragon's wine souffle.

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:15.990
To bring out all its flavor,
I'll add a special...

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:19.500
...wine to it and pressure
cook it for two weeks!

00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:21.660
Two WEEKS?!

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:24.440
Okay, fine.
I can wait that long.

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:28.380
At which point I'll need a
month to make the special sauce.

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:29.880
A... A MONTH?!

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:32.970
Won't it rot if you do that?

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:35.810
A dragon's life
force isn't that weak!

00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:36.980
If your ingredients are fresh...

00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:39.680
...they'll keep for all
six months of cooking!

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:41.750
SIX MONTHS?!

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:43.690
This is top class dragon
cuisine I'm making here!

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:46.250
Making it and eating it
is serious business!

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:47.890
We can't wait that long.

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:49.990
We'll just have
to forget about it.

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:52.470
I thought the orc
meat was just fine.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:53.600
How about dragon's fin soup?!

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:56.570
It takes two months of
boiling to make the broth.

00:19:57.140 --> 00:19:58.300
What about shabu-shabu?

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:02.310
You have to boil it
continuously for three months.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:06.650
Okay, sashimi! If you don't have
to cook it, I can eat it now, right?

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.120
We'd have to bury it in
the ground for three months...

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:11.380
...to leech the poison out
of the meat or you'd die.

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:14.250
Fine, I'll die!
I'm gonna eat it!

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:16.160
I am DEFINITELY
going to eat it!

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:18.630
No, you can't!

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:20.890
No choice.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:23.330
Come on, let me eat it!
Just a little! Come on!

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:26.200
Hey! Hey, guys, stop it!
What are you doing?!

00:20:26.270 --> 00:20:27.800
It's really a shame, isn't it?

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.400
We'll see you later.

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:33.100
For the sake of Justice,
we must travel on!

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:36.170
Justice is me getting to eat
dragon cuisine! Come on, guys!

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:36.940
See you.

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:42.250
Come on, just a little!
Guys, please! We HAVE to eat it!

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:59.640
Give me...
Give me my dragon cuisine!
